From ca7799841f06da429e50a236d7e0b5c5091e99e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 10:58:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build: Do not force an 8 byte output section alignment for
 clang

LINKCMDS_ALIGN_DIRECTIVE stands in for ALIGN_WITH_INPUT, which lld cannot
parse.  The clang option spec substituted ALIGN(8), but ALIGN_WITH_INPUT
only ties the alignment of an output section's LMA to that of its VMA, it
does not impose an alignment.  The faithful substitute is nothing at all.

Forcing ALIGN(8) changes the meaning of the TLS block.  With .tbss aligned
to 8 rather than to its natural alignment, _TLS_Size is computed as
_TLS_BSS_end - _TLS_Data_begin over the padding, so a single one-byte
thread-local reports a size of 8.  sptls01 checks for exactly this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 spec/build/bsps/optclang.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/spec/build/bsps/optclang.yml b/spec/build/bsps/optclang.yml
index f67b004a37..60ecca89eb 100644
--- a/spec/build/bsps/optclang.yml
+++ b/spec/build/bsps/optclang.yml
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
 actions:
 - set-value: INPUT
 - env-assign: LINKCMDS_START_DIRECTIVE
-- set-value: ALIGN(8)
+- set-value: ''
 - env-assign: LINKCMDS_ALIGN_DIRECTIVE
 build-type: option
 copyrights:
